          "body": "### Describe the feature\n\n## Premise\n\nreadQuery() as it is currently only works if you either\n\n1. have extremely simple data - basically exclusively strings.\n2. make a custom schema with coercing (assuming the validation library supports everything needed) for every API endpoint, not really being able to reuse existing schemas\n3. send all data as body payload (this wouldn't be a problem if GET and DELETE were allowed to have bodies)\n4. send all data as stringified JSON\n5. or (like me) make a shim that tries its best at adjusting the data to better fit a schema\n\nnone of these options are particularly enticing, so (imo) there should be a system to somehow fix this in h3.\n\n## My shim/workaround\n\nwithout posting code, I basically crawl through the zod type definition alongside the passed data and adjust the data where it can't be unambiguously represented by query parameters.\n\nI'm not sure how viable this is for h3 considering it's supposed to be somewhat validator-agnostic… But then again, having this feature for a limited amount of libraries would be better than having it for none at all.\n\n## Additional notes\n\nzod has already declined to implement a version of this on their side: https://github.com/colinhacks/zod/issues/2873\n\n### Additional information\n\n- [ ] Would you be willing to help implement this feature?",
