          "body": "### Environment\n\nh3@2.0.1-rc.30\n\n### Reproduction\n\nhttps://stackblitz.com/edit/unjs-h3-pqkunrof?file=server.ts\n\n### Describe the bug\n\nA [recent change](https://github.com/h3js/h3/commit/69ec3c73bc2b2f5086023a5fb3e7bd9a201b0f00#diff-d78b1387942039c256ea6ebde5c7c623105390c7972d3dcfaaf8c10a0f620ad1R8) to the `HTTPHandler` type now explicitly passes `any` to type generic parameters, causing the shape to raise `typescript-eslint` errors for strictness (specifically the `@typescript-eslint/no-unsafe-argument` rule).\n\nThe specific use case flagging this rule is a common case of passing an event handler `event` to another internal H3 function:\n\n```ts\nimport { H3, proxyRequest } from 'h3';\n\nconst app = new H3();\n//                                   ⌄ H3Event<EventHandlerRequest> expected\napp.get('/', (event) => proxyRequest(event, '/test'));\n//            ^ H3Event<any> passed\n\nexport default app;\n```\n\nESLint output:\n\n```shell\n> lint\n> eslint\n\n\n/home/projects/unjs-h3-pqkunrof/server.ts\n  5:38  error  Unsafe argument of type `H3Event<any>` assigned to a parameter of type `H3Event<EventHandlerRequest>`  @typescript-eslint/no-unsafe-argument\n\n✖ 1 problem (1 error, 0 warnings)\n```\n\n### Additional context\n\nWondering if the explicit `any` being passed can be omitted entirely, or if this is something needed, the issue can be closed with wontfix and I can disable this lint rule in my projects.\n\nThanks!\n\n### Logs\n\n```sh\n\n```",
